WEBVTT

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:22.080
Thank you for coming to our wedding, everyone.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:29.000
I'm so happy that I'm about
to marry the person I love.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.200
It's thanks to my brother,
who put all this together in a single day,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.250
that I'm able to hold such a wonderful wedding.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.700
Thank you again, brother!

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:41.830
Thank you!

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.700
Huh? Brother?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.870
What the hell is this?

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.700
Overcome by the atmosphere of the banquet,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.370
you party more than anyone.
You drink more than anyone.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:15.830
That doesn't sound like a good idea
for a man who has to run ten leagues.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:20.200
You weren't planning on not going back, right?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.870
Are you just going to abandon them?

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.700
Your friend who waits for you
at the dwelling place of the king.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.620
How did you know?

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.450
There's no time.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.200
Before you start asking questions...

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.500
Run, Melos.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.460
"Episode 1"

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.580
What were you going to do with that dagger?

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.330
Save the city from a tyrant!

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.870
You?

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.830
I've been told...

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.910
...that you can't believe in anyone.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.200
So you make the people suffer, and kill them!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.450
A king like you can't be allowed to live!

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:43.040
You would dare attempt to slay a king?

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.370
Kill this impudent man now!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.580
Wait...

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.620
Wait, your highness.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.830
He has a younger sister.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:58.830
Can you let him see his sister before he dies?

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.790
You're telling me to release him?

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.290
No!

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.950
If I do, he'll run away.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.000
Then I'll stay here in his place.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:19.790
If he doesn't come back,
you can kill me instead!

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.200
My friend...

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.870
No, I can't abandon him!

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.250
Of course, I was going to run right back!

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.250
But I couldn't help myself
when I saw all that mead...

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.700
It's true that I hesitated.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.790
Did you see my sister's happy face?

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:42.540
I'm going back to die!

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.120
If I die, I'll never see her again!

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.200
How could someone not hesitate
in the face of that smile?

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.160
And you should be running, too!

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.040
No.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.910
Running tires me.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.040
It's not fair that only I have to run!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.540
That's how the story goes, though.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.200
Story?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.790
You're being weird.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:09.500
How did you know about
my promise with the king, anyway?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.040
Were you watching somewhere?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.830
"Watching" is not the right way to put it.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.160
But I'll say this:

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.580
it's always simpler for someone on the outside

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.620
to understand what's really going on.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.870
That's not an answer!

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.830
Jeez... This is not the time for this!

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:31.370
I'm sympathetic, but...

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.330
I think you do have a share
of responsibility in this.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.370
I can understand your rage
at the king's tyranny.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:44.580
But does that make it okay
to just attempt to kill him?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.580
You're a little over-emotional, aren't you?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.450
Huh?!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.870
See? You got mad again! Melos got mad again!

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.450
You make me so mad!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.790
Now... I think it's about time.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.370
Oh, no!

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.500
I no longer hesitate in my desire
to save my friend,

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.700
but now I must face this trial!

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.000
It's not fair!

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.450
Forgive me, Selinuntius!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.700
I did everything I could,

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.080
but this raging torrent stymies me!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.120
What the hell?

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.500
A cloud thread.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.620
If you have something that helpful,
then show it to me earlier!

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.000
No, I won't say that.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.580
Now, use that thread to help me get over.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.250
No, I can't do that.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.290
What?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:45.410
You're about to give your utmost
in trying to cross this river.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:46.450
Impossible!

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.540
You want me to swim through this torrent?

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.750
I'll die!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.250
I think you'll be fine.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:55.620
Good luck!

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.160
H-Help me! Help!

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.450
He's gone!

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.410
I'll kill that bastard!

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:39.370
Hey.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.750
Give us everything you've got.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.000
I'm sorry, friend.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.290
I can still make it!

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.700
Wait for me, Selinuntius!

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.290
I'm coming back!

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.950
I promised my friend!

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.620
I can't betray his trust!

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.910
Betray...

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.910
King! I've returned!

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.450
What are you doing here, Melos?

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.160
You know why I'm here!

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.750
I came to save my friend!

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.830
Who is your friend?

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.040
Do you mean this man?

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.330
What?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.910
Look carefully!

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.750
Is he truly your friend?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.870
Is he worthy of saving?

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:51.950
Selinuntius!

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.870
My friend!

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:57.290
No... You're...

00:08:58.620 --> 00:08:59.830
You're...

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.000
Why?

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.500
Why are you here?

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.790
You betrayed me!

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.250
Yes, Melos.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:14.000
He betrayed you. He's not worth saving.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.000
So...

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.620
Kill him!

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.250
With your own hands!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.540
You want me to...?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.750
Yes. Just like that.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.660
This world will disappear,
ending in a story of betrayal!

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.620
I'm sorry, but that's changing
the story a little too much.

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.160
You're...

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.250
A tragedy is fine.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:54.870
But there's nothing worse than
taking a story that should end happily

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.700
and turning it into a tragedy.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.370
You can't be...

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.200
Who are these guys?

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.790
The Taints.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.750
You should get back.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.410
Wow...

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.290
Who are you?

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.750
Can't you tell?

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.580
Just an author.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.700
A delver. I knew it.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.500
But I won't let you interfere!

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:58.410
Oww...

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:02.620
No!

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.450
Dazai.

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.500
S-Sensei?

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.910
It's good to see you again, Dazai.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:27.910
I never thought we'd get the chance.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.950
You recognize this hospital room, right?

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:35.000
You would come here often
for your morphine addiction.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.290
I...

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.540
You still don't understand?

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:41.080
You're Osamu Dazai.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:44.620
The student of Haruo Sato, myself.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:47.580
I guess you could say that, anyway.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.950
You don't remember?

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.910
No, I do. Kind of.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:54.450
I see.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:12:01.080
Sensei, you knew I wanted
the Akutagawa Prize, right?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:06.410
Yeah. You admired Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.330
And I still think that your

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:15.330
<i>Against the Current</i> was worthy
to win the first Akutagawa prize.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.290
But I couldn't get it.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.870
It couldn't be helped.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:22.200
I wasn't the only judge.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:26.580
But you said I could get it next time, right?

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:29.080
I believed those words!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:32.410
That's why I kept telling you
to give me the prize!

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.370
But...

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:37.540
Next time, you weren't even a finalist.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:42.370
I see. You consider that
as a betrayal on my part.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.250
Can you say it's not?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:46.620
I can't.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.790
Not as long as you feel that way.

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:54.330
Because of you,
I became unable to believe in anyone!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.410
I start to think that I might be betrayed again!

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:05.910
Listen, Dazai. I blame myself
for your inability to believe in others.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.910
But it's your problem, and yours alone.

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:13.910
You are you. Your works are your work.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:16.000
Don't forget that.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:19.040
Sensei! Sensei!

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.120
Sensei!

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:25.620
I'm not your sensei.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.080
You!

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.830
Hey, tell me already!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.410
What's going on here?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.500
What am I doing here?
Why am I dressed like this?

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:42.790
Seems like you've started
to remember, Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.660
I'll tell you, then.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:49.700
We're inside a book written
by Osamu Dazai. That is, you.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.120
Inside a book?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:55.040
The book's title is <i>Run, Melos</i> .

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.750
<i>Run, Melos</i> ?

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.120
Did I write that?

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.700
I can understand that you wouldn't
be able to remember.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:09.120
When an author enters a book,
they forget everything about it.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.620
This world is filled with countless books.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:17.250
But there are those who
would destroy these books.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.830
The Taints.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.870
Taints?

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.290
When the Taints set their sights on a book,

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.870
the soul of the author
who wrote it is trapped within.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:30.080
Just like you are.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:35.080
Then, they change the contents
of the book before destroying it.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.450
I don't get it!

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.580
What are you saying?

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:43.200
How can we defeat those monsters?

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.660
I'm surprised.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.700
You intend to defeat them?

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:47.870
We're not going to?

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.080
It's not easy.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.200
But will you listen?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.870
Sensei!

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:58.830
Dazai.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.700
There's only one way to destroy the Taints.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:05.200
Lead the story to its proper conclusion.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:08.370
The theme of <i>Run, Melos</i> is belief.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:13.120
Thus, you must believe in another in the end,
and your belief must be justified.

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:14.120
Run.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.620
There you are.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.620
Rot, Melos.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.410
Oww!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.450
Are you trying to kill me?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.750
Don't worry.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:43.040
An author can't die inside their book.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.910
But you can.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.200
True.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:50.700
But whether you can kill me
is a different matter.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.120
This is a bit of a problem.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.790
Sensei...

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:32.500
I may not be able to believe in others anymore.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:39.910
That's how much your betrayal affected my heart.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:42.250
But really, I...

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:47.450
Why, Sensei?

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:51.910
I'm not the only judge for the Akutagawa Prize.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.750
Some things just can't be helped.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:59.950
<i>Flowers of Buffoonery</i> was a splendid book.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:05.330
You can do more, I believe.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.040
I believe in you...

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.660
"You believe in me."

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:13.200
I wanted to be a man who believed in that,
who could run straight forward!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.950
And because I couldn't do it myself...

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.000
Instead, I was able to put
those feelings into my work!

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:23.830
That's what it means to be an author!

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:24.830
Dazai!

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:31.120
Right now, I'm Melos!

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:37.000
I'm sorry I kept you waiting, my friend.

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:06.750
The story of trust has been completed, it seems.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.200
You lose.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.700
I refuse to accept it! I refuse!

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:13.870
You're pretty pathetic.

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:16.870
Just admit your defeat.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:20.790
But if you say you can't...

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:38.080
...I'll finish you off myself!

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.870
Seems it's time to say goodbye.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:07.330
Well, you kind of pissed me off.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.790
But you helped me out a lot.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:12.500
I didn't do anything to help you.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.120
I just protected the book.

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.250
Oh, yeah?

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:21.200
Hey, will we meet again?

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.200
The return was a success.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:34.450
Huh? How?

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:37.500
Huh? Where am I?

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.410
You're back.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:42.450
This is our home and base.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.330
Something like that, anyway.

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:45.870
Why am I here too?

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:51.120
When you defeat the Taints,
the author is released from the book.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.540
Didn't I tell you?

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.950
No!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.370
So what was all that about saying goodbye?

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.580
Goodbye to the world of the book, I meant.

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.290
How was I supposed to know that?

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:01.500
How embarrassing!

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.540
I thought I was saying my last goodbye!

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:08.080
Let's go to the Director's room.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:10.700
This is the Director's room?

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.290
Nobody's here.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:15.370
Welcome, Osamu Dazai.

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.790
I'm right here.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.790
A c-cat?

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.500
He's the acting Director.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.080
And our boss.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.370
A cat is?

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:26.080
First, good job purifying that book.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:28.830
The author was a handful. I'm tired.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.580
A talking cat...

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:34.450
Even after becoming an astral being,
his personality hasn't improved, huh?

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:35.950
Astral being?

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:39.450
You are Dazai. But not Dazai.

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:44.120
A phantasm, created from
the image of Osamu Dazai.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:49.910
Otherwise, authors from different eras
wouldn't be able to gather in one place.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:51.750
I don't understand,

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:55.870
but is it maybe the same way Haruo- <i>sensei</i>
was able to be inside my book?

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:57.750
Haruo Sato?

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:58.910
Yes.

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:00.750
It's the same principal.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:07.870
But the Haruo Sato you saw in the book
was just a phantasm, created by Dazai.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:12.540
The best way to destroy the book <i>Run, Melos</i>

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:15.580
was for Melos to abandon his friend.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.620
And he was there to allow that to happen.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:20.870
Yes.

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:24.540
If Dazai became Melos,
who would he be most likely to abandon?

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:28.410
That was the answer the Taints
pulled from Dazai's memory.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.620
The Taints can do that?

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.500
They're very smart.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:35.160
And thus, a threat.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:37.790
What are the Taints, anyway?

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:39.870
Why do they want to destroy books?

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:41.620
We don't know.

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:45.910
Why do they try to taint and destroy books?

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:49.120
There may be no reason.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:52.080
That would be the worst case.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:58.160
But we can't let the books be destroyed.

00:21:58.160 --> 00:22:04.120
Books, and literature,
are a necessary part of a good life.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:07.910
If all books disappeared from this world,

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:10.700
civilization would collapse,

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:13.540
and human history would end.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:15.370
Human history would end?

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:18.200
Our job is to stop that.

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:23.080
Only authors who created literature
can defeat the Taints.

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.620
That means you.

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:31.120
Osamu Dazai, you're going
to help us fight the Taints.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.580
I'm going to fight the Taints?

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:36.620
You've created many fine works.

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:39.790
I know you won't stand by
when literature is in peril.

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:40.700
I don't really care, actually.

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:41.500
You don't?

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:44.370
Why do authors fight, anyway?

00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:47.660
I was swinging a scythe around back there, sure.

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:50.580
But why do I have a weapon anyway?

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:51.660
I'm an author!

00:22:51.660 --> 00:22:55.250
Well, you've got me there.

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:57.660
You really are fun, Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:02.290
Hey, Akutagawa. Stop laughing and say something.

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:03.620
Akutagawa?

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:08.040
Don't scream.

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:11.620
Akutagawa? No way...

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:15.450
<i>The</i> Ryunosuke Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:17.370
I didn't tell you?

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:19.370
I'm Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:21.330
Nice to meet you, Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:30.910
"Run, Melos"

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:35.010
"Literary Gourmet!

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:35.010
'Beloved Crab Croquettes.'"

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.520
"Step step"

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:38.660
I can't believe I got to meet Ryunosuke Akutagawa!

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:42.290
But I'm hungry...

00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:46.540
This is what I need!

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:51.570
"Crab Croquettes: Croquettes filled with crab meat.
Crunchy on the outside, creamy in the middle."

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:48.700
Delicious breading! Soft cream!

00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:51.540
Filled with yummy crab, just like you'd hope for!

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:57.160
Is Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> eating yellowtail teriyaki?

00:23:57.160 --> 00:23:59.410
Excuse me! Give me yellowtail teriyaki!

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:01.660
Eat your own meal first!
